   "The work-order-page behaviour the case checks (a refused change shows an error, the old lead stays) is not changed by v68; §4 still lists 'the work order detail page' among the paths that must refuse the change.",
   "One quote is out of date: 'PRD §4 Key Decisions (lead lock)' quotes the v33-era sentence ('— board drag, Reassign dialog, and the work order detail page.'). v68 reads '— board drag, the lead technician dialog, Unassign, Undo, and the work order detail page.' Rule 113 would re-quote it, but the QA lead's 19 Oct order freezes the Expected field; left for his decision (see questions).",
